      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "card_count, call_count = map(int, input().split())\nvisible = list(input())\nhidden = list(input())\nfor called in input():\n    for index in range(card_count):\n        if visible[index] == called:\n            visible[index], hidden[index] = hidden[index], visible[index]\nprint(\"\".join(visible))\n",
      "statement": "There are [[card_count]] cards in a fixed order.\n\nEach card has a letter on the front and a letter on the back.\n\nThe string [[front]] contains the front letters of the cards.\nThe string [[back]] contains the back letters in the same order.\n\nAt the beginning, all cards show their front side.\n\nRead the [[calls]] from left to right.\n\nFor each called letter, flip every card that is currently showing that letter.\n\nEach card can be flipped only once for the same call, even if both sides have the same letter.\n\nOnly the letter currently visible on a card matters. The hidden letter does not affect the current call.\n\nAfter all calls, print [[visible_faces]], the visible letters in card order.",
